  <section class="np-lead" id="build">
    <div class="np-shell">
      <p class="np-kicker" data-ink style="--press-delay: 400ms">Dispatch from the composing room</p>
      <h2 class="np-headline" data-ink style="--press-delay: 440ms">
        Your browser now holds a complete <em>printing press</em>
      </h2>
      <p class="np-deck" data-ink style="--press-delay: 520ms">
        PDF Studio composes invoices, letters, proposals and CVs on a true page grid — then exports a
        genuine PDF with the fonts embedded. No account, no upload queue, no cloud lock-in.
      </p>
      <p class="np-byline" data-ink style="--press-delay: 580ms">
        <span>By <b>the editors</b></span>
        <span>Filed under Tools</span>
        <span>Reading time 3 min</span>
      </p>

      <div class="np-lead-grid">
        <div class="np-lead-copy" data-ink style="--press-delay: 640ms">
          <div class="np-columns">
            <p>
              <span class="np-dropcap" aria-hidden="true">M</span>ost document tools ask for an email
              address before they will let you draw a rectangle. This one asks for nothing. Open the
              editor and a blank A4 sheet is already waiting, ruled and ready for copy.
            </p>
            <p>
              Everything happens on the page itself. Text blocks, tables, images, shapes and
              signatures sit against real page coordinates, with smart guides that snap to the margins
              you actually care about. Zoom in to set a caption; zoom out to judge the whole spread.
            </p>
            <p>
              When the layout is right, the export is not a screenshot of the screen. pdf-lib writes a
              genuine file — correct page size, embedded fonts, selectable text — the kind of PDF a
              printer or a client accepts without argument.
            </p>
            <p>
              And the draft never leaves the machine it was typed on.
              <b>Nothing is uploaded in order to start working.</b>
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="np-actions">
            <a href="/editor?new=1" class="np-btn np-btn--ink">Start a blank sheet</a>
            <a href="/editor?template=invoice" class="np-btn np-btn--outline">Open the invoice</a>
          </div>
        </div>

        <figure class="np-plate-fig" data-plate>
          <div class="np-plate">
