  <section class="np-section" id="oped">
    <div class="np-shell">
      <div class="np-oped" data-reveal>
        <p class="np-oped-slug">From the editors</p>
        <h2 class="np-oped-title">Your documents do not leave this machine</h2>
        <div class="np-oped-body">
          <p>
            <span class="np-dropcap" aria-hidden="true">T</span>here is a quiet assumption in modern
            software that your work belongs on somebody else's server. We do not share it. PDF Studio
            is local-first, and it stays that way by default.
          </p>
          <p>
            Drafts are held in this browser session. There is no account to create, no workspace to
            join, and no upload step standing between you and a finished page. Close the tab and the
            work is where you left it, on your own disk.
          </p>
          <p>
            The PDF you export is a file, not a link. It is yours to send, print or archive, with the
            fonts travelling inside it so the document renders the same on whatever machine opens it
            next.
          </p>
        </div>
        <p class="np-oped-sign">— The editors, PDF Studio</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

